  "status_text": "One extra bit flip makes every coloring fit. For any finite graph and quota b, Lean checked a construction with three lights whose rules take at least b NOTs. At b, the lights can show exactly the proper three-colorings, where neighbors use different colors. At b+1, every assignment of three colors can be shown. For n vertices and m=2(2^b-1), there are 14n+m tested inputs, and each promised assignment has a circuit within 100(n+m+1) total gates (L-lib-1289).",
